# Code owner of the repository.
#
# Paired with the "require_code_owner_reviews" setting of the `master` branch
# protection, this file has a precise effect: a pull request can only be merged
# with an approval **from this account**. An approval from another contributor,
# even one with write access, does not unblock it.
#
# That is what makes it possible to hand out branch-push rights widely while
# keeping a single hand on what enters `master`.
#
# GitHub offers no direct restriction of pushes to a branch on a personal
# repository — "Only organization repositories can have users and team
# restrictions" — hence this detour, which achieves the same result.

